                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3e6e4c55-4938-47cb-be8d-02adc3e2f3cf",
                        "source_entry_id": "df762c99-68a4-3e54-8802-a1b1088d4a20",
                        "target_lang_word": "massaranduba",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "massaranduba",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cec9ebff-2f36-3ca7-b560-70eec2eb40cd",
                                        "entry_id": "5fd6c4bc-cbed-3ae3-b06e-4801a7c6cca4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tropical hardwood tree, Manilkara bidentata, which produces edible fruit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce9aa18f-5789-4803-acce-c0d263dd55f7",
                                                "sense_id": "cec9ebff-2f36-3ca7-b560-70eec2eb40cd",
                                                "text": "The famous polo de vaca, or \"cow-tree\" of South America, called massaranduba by the natives, belongs to the natural order of the Atrocarpads, which, by what might appear a curious coincidence, includes also the celebrated bread-fruit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3eda547-30e0-4475-801c-6c62d2a042d7",
                                                "sense_id": "cec9ebff-2f36-3ca7-b560-70eec2eb40cd",
                                                "text": "The massaranduba is not the only species known as palo de vaca, or cow-tree. There are many others so called, whose sap is of a milky nature."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0a4486f-07a9-4f5e-b46b-020948fb747a",
                                                "sense_id": "cec9ebff-2f36-3ca7-b560-70eec2eb40cd",
                                                "text": "Then the huge reddish trunks of massarandubas began to slide past us, their lofty crowns matting together so thickly that they seemed to make a solid roof."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
